DeepFake-Guard 🛡️

An image-based deepfake detection pipeline built in a Jupyter/Google Colab notebook. It trains and compares two models — a lightweight custom CNN (MesoNet) and a transfer-learning model (EfficientNet-B4) — on a balanced real-vs-fake face dataset, then serves predictions through a simple Gradio web demo.

📌 Overview
Task: Binary image classification — Real face vs. Fake (deepfake) face
Dataset: real-vs-fake face dataset (balanced, ~10k real + ~10k fake images used from the test split), loaded from Google Drive
Models:
MesoNet — a small custom CNN (4 conv blocks, ~28K parameters) trained from scratch
EfficientNet-B4 — ImageNet-pretrained backbone with a custom classification head, trained via transfer learning
Environment: Google Colab (GPU runtime recommended)
Demo: Gradio-based web interface for uploading an image and getting a Real/Fake prediction
DeepFake-Guard/
└── real_vs_fake/
    └── real-vs-fake/
        └── test/
            ├── real/
            └── fake/
Pipeline
Data loading — Walks Google Drive to locate real/ and fake/ folders, builds a Pandas dataframe of file paths + labels.
Preprocessing & augmentation — ImageDataGenerator with rescaling, rotation, zoom, flips, shifts, and brightness jitter for the training set; plain rescaling for validation/test.
Model building:
build_mesonet() — custom CNN with Conv2D + BatchNorm + MaxPooling blocks, dropout, and a sigmoid output.
build_efficientnet_b4() — frozen EfficientNet-B4 base (ImageNet weights) + GlobalAveragePooling2D + Dense head with L2 regularization and dropout.
Training — Both models trained with Adam optimizer, binary cross-entropy loss, and callbacks: ModelCheckpoint, EarlyStopping, ReduceLROnPlateau, CSVLogger.
Local caching — Images are copied from Drive to local Colab disk (/content/data) to speed up training I/O.
Evaluation — Confusion matrices, ROC curves, and standard classification metrics (accuracy, AUC, F1, precision, recall).
Demo — A Gradio interface (automated_forensic_scan) for uploading an image and getting a prediction.

Getting Started
